
@startuml PayLink_Refund_Failed_Payment

title PayLink - Sequence Diagram: Refund a Failed Payment

autonumber

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

actor Customer

participant "Payment API" as API
participant "Payment Processing\nService" as Payment
participant "Wallet & Hold\nService" as Wallet
participant "Ledger Service" as Ledger
participant "Biller Adapter" as Adapter
participant "Biller" as Biller
participant "Notification Service" as Notify
participant "SMS Provider" as SMS
participant "Push Provider" as Push

== Payment Initiation ==

Customer -> API : Confirm payment(paymentId)
API -> Payment : processPayment(paymentId)

Payment -> Wallet : placeHold(walletId, totalAmount)
Wallet -> Ledger : record hold movement
Ledger --> Wallet : Ledger entries created
Wallet --> Payment : Hold placed successfully

Payment -> Payment : Change status to FundsHeld
Payment -> Adapter : sendPayment(paymentReference,\ntotalAmount)
Adapter -> Biller : Submit payment request

== Biller Response ==

Biller --> Adapter : Payment rejected(errorCode,\nreason)
Adapter --> Payment : Payment failed(errorCode,\nreason)

Payment -> Payment : Validate current payment state
Payment -> Payment : Update status:\nSentToBiller -> Failed
Payment -> Payment : Save Payment Event

== Release Held Funds ==

Payment -> Wallet : releaseHold(paymentId)
Wallet -> Wallet : Verify hold is active\nand not already released

Wallet -> Ledger : Record release movements
Ledger -> Ledger : Debit held balance\nCredit available balance
Ledger --> Wallet : Ledger entries saved

Wallet -> Wallet : Mark hold as Released
Wallet --> Payment : Hold released successfully

Payment -> Payment : Update status:\nFailed -> Refunded
Payment -> Payment : Save Payment Event

== Notify Customer ==

Payment -> Notify : sendFailureNotification(\npaymentReference, reason)

par SMS Notification
    Notify -> SMS : Send SMS(failure reason,\nrefund confirmation)
    SMS --> Notify : Delivery result
else Push Notification
    Notify -> Push : Send push notification\n(failure and refund status)
    Push --> Notify : Delivery result
end

Notify --> Payment : Notification requests processed
Payment --> API : Return Refunded status
API --> Customer : Show payment failed\nand funds returned

note over Payment, Wallet
  Refund is completed only after
  the hold is successfully released.

  The payment lifecycle is:
  SentToBiller -> Failed -> Refunded
end note

note over Wallet, Ledger
  Wallet balances are derived from
  ledger entries.

  Every money movement must be recorded.
  The available balance increases and
  the held balance decreases.
end note

note over Payment, Biller
  If the biller does not respond within
  10 seconds, the payment becomes Unknown.
  Funds remain held until the biller outcome
  is confirmed. No automatic refund occurs.
end note

@enduml
